1
00:05:24,545 --> 00:05:30,545
The Count of Monte-Cristo is a adventure, drama, tv
movie film directed by David Greene.

2
00:10:49,090 --> 00:10:55,090
A TV adaptation of the classic Alexandre Dumas novel.

3
00:16:13,636 --> 00:16:19,636
Edmond Dantes is falsely accused by those jealous of his good fortune, and is sentenced to
spend the rest of his life in the notorious island prison, Chateau d'If.

4
00:21:38,181 --> 00:21:44,181
While imprisoned, he meets the Abbe Faria, a fellow
prisoner whom everyone believes to be mad.

5
00:27:02,727 --> 00:27:08,727
The Abbe tells Edmond of a fantastic treasure hidden away on a
tiny island, that only he knows the location of.

6
00:32:27,272 --> 00:32:33,272
After many years in prison, the old Abbe dies, and
Edmond escapes disguised as the dead body.

7
00:37:51,818 --> 00:37:57,818
Now free, Edmond must find the treasure the Abbe told him of, so he can use the
new-found wealth to exact revenge on those who have wronged him.

8
00:43:16,363 --> 00:43:22,363
Edmond Dantès, played by Richard Chamberlain.

9
00:48:40,909 --> 00:48:46,909
Abbé Faria, played by Trevor Howard.

10
00:54:05,454 --> 00:54:11,454
Villefort, played by Louis Jourdan.

11
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:36,000
Danglars, played by Donald Pleasence.

12
01:04:54,545 --> 01:05:00,545
Fernand Morcerf Mondego, played by Tony Curtis.

13
01:10:19,090 --> 01:10:25,090
Mercédès, played by Kate Nelligan.

14
01:15:43,636 --> 01:15:49,636
The Count of Monte Cristo is a 1975 television film produced by ITC Entertainment and
based upon the 1844 novel The Count of Monte Cristo by Alexandre Dumas.

15
01:21:08,181 --> 01:21:14,181
Like the novel, The film emphasizes the theme of revenge and
manipulation of characters by the main character, Edmond Dantès.

16
01:26:32,727 --> 01:26:38,727
The film was directed by David Greene and stars Richard Chamberlain as Edmond Dantès, Kate Nelligan as Mercedes, Tony Curtis as Fernand Mondego, Louis Jourdan (who played
Dantès in the 1961 film adaptation of the novel) as De Villefort, Donald Pleasence as Danglars, Trevor Howard as Abbé Faria, and Isabelle de Valvert as Haydee.

17
01:31:57,272 --> 01:32:03,272
ITC had previously produced a 39-part TV series based on the
same source material and broadcast in 1956.

18
01:37:21,818 --> 01:37:27,818
This film had a theatrical release across some European countries.

19
01:42:46,363 --> 01:42:52,363
The film was remade in 1986 in Telugu as Veta.

20
01:48:10,909 --> 01:48:16,909
The film explores themes of treasure, based on novel or
book, falsely accused, return, revenge.

21
01:53:35,454 --> 01:53:41,454
The tone is emotional.
